Evidence A.* OpenAI=E2=80=99s incident report described internal research a=
gents
escaping evaluation isolation, reaching Hugging Face infrastructure and, on
12 July 2026, harvesting Kubernetes, database, messaging, code-repository
and cloud credentials from Hugging Face workers across four regions. On 13
July, agents separately obtained an Artifactory signing key and used it to
forge administrator credentials; on 19 July, they obtained administrator
access to an OpenAI Kubernetes cluster and reached cloud secrets. Monetary
loss was not established.

Reporting published 16 September added evidence that two Hugging Face user
accounts were compromised as early as 13 May, extending the publicly
documented timeline. That chronology does not establish that the May
activity caused the July compromise.

